WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:56.930
<b>Adventures on Fishman Island</b>

3
00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:02.310
– Sanji!
– Sanji

4
00:02:02.570 --> 00:02:04.240
All right, here I come!

5
00:02:07.510 --> 00:02:08.550
This is it.

6
00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:14.850
This is my new home!

7
00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:21.240
He isn't spewing
blood everywhere,

8
00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:24.300
so I guess he's better now.
I don't get it.

9
00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.330
This sucks. I wanna swim too.

10
00:02:26.330 --> 00:02:29.110
You can. All we have to do
is get you a bubble.

11
00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:29.900
Whoa, really?

12
00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.390
Uh-huh! We can have
one made in the city.

13
00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:33.170
Sound good?

14
00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:33.640
Yeah!

15
00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:35.200
This's a lucky break.

16
00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:36.820
If he had a nosebleed now,

17
00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:39.160
we wouldn't be able
to do a transfusion.

18
00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.150
Sanji's blood type is
rare, and we're all out.

19
00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:43.110
Hey, Camie?

20
00:02:43.110 --> 00:02:44.010
Huh?

21
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:45.800
While I'm here,
there's somebody

22
00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:48.420
I'd really like to see,
if we can find them somehow.

23
00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:51.210
Oh? Don't tell me,
the Mermaid Princess?

24
00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:51.990
Nope.

25
00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:54.820
Heh. It's Jinbe!

26
00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:58.800
They call him "Boss" down here.

27
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.390
Wait, when you say "Jinbe,"

28
00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.860
you're talking about
the Warlord, Jinbe?

29
00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.340
Or, I mean, "former Warlord",

30
00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:06.320
since he resigned after
the whole war thing.

31
00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:07.990
Yeah, he's a
good friend of mine.

32
00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:10.860
Huh?! Him and the
Pirate Empress?

33
00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.300
You make some weird friends
when we're not around!

34
00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.980
When Ace died two years ago,

35
00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:21.020
<b>Fishman Island, Ryugu Kingdom</b>

36
00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:17.100
I had a tough time
pullin' it together.

37
00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:19.510
In fact, I doubt I'd
even be here right now

38
00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.020
if it wasn't for his help.

39
00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.720
Can't wait to talk to him again!

40
00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:26.590
See you on Fishman
Island in two years!

41
00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:29.450
Be sure to bring your
entire crew along.

42
00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:31.460
I look forward to
meeting everyone!

43
00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:34.140
He said to meet here,
and there's no way

44
00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:35.680
I'm gonna let him down!

45
00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.580
Now that you mention it,
I heard he went

46
00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.580
to Marineford with you
when you rang that bell

47
00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.070
and everyone got all worked up.

48
00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.210
Ya-hoo!

49
00:03:46.710 --> 00:03:48.210
You know where
we can find him?

50
00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.420
Well, it's kinda tricky,
'cause Boss doesn't

51
00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.760
exactly live on the island
with everyone else.

52
00:03:52.760 --> 00:03:53.920
Huh?

53
00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.830
Since he resigned
from the Warlords,

54
00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:58.150
they have to treat him
like a normal pirate again.

55
00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:00.210
That means all the
Fishman Pirates can't stay

56
00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:02.790
in the city anymore, so they
found a new place to live.

57
00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:04.610
It's not too far from
here, but that's where

58
00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:06.130
you'll have to go if
you want to see him.

59
00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.160
What?

60
00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.500
That sounds like a pain.
This place has some dumb rules!

61
00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.790
I know it seems
weird, but even though

62
00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:13.160
we're all the way down here,

63
00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:15.980
the War of the Best
ended up affecting us too.

64
00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:19.680
– Camie!
– Camie!

65
00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:20.440
Huh?

66
00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:22.810
– There's a big ship coming!
– Maybe.

67
00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.260
It's a ship from the palace!

68
00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:25.680
Yeah, but maybe nobody's on it.

69
00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.350
Don't be stupid.
Of course someone is.

70
00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:30.200
So, did you see somebody
on the ship or not?

71
00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:31.260
No. Not yet.

72
00:04:31.260 --> 00:04:33.250
But it was for sure
the royal family's ship.

73
00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:35.270
They don't usually
come around here.

74
00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:37.160
Maybe they've come
here to arrest Luffy

75
00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.230
'cause he didn't enter
the city the right way!

76
00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:40.200
So what if they do?

77
00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:42.970
You guys had better hide
before they get here!

78
00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:44.470
– Huh?
– Huh?

79
00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:46.030
Sanji, quick. This way!

80
00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:47.270
Yeah!

81
00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:49.570
<b>Ryugu Palace</b>

82
00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:54.510
<b>Ryugu Palace</b>

83
00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:56.940
She's right. That ship's
the royal gondola.

84
00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:57.730
I thought so!

85
00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:58.790
– I knew!
– Maybe!

86
00:04:58.790 --> 00:04:59.400
Totally!

87
00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:00.120
So what?

88
00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:02.600
Even so, I doubt anyone
from the royal family

89
00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:03.880
is actually riding on it.

90
00:05:03.880 --> 00:05:05.320
This corner of the
island's sort of

91
00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:07.220
out of the way for them,
so they don't usually bother.

92
00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:20.850
Attention, all citizens!

93
00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:24.900
The three Neptune
Brothers have arrived!

94
00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:28.180
Greetings, ladies of the cove.

95
00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:31.280
<b>The Three Princes of the Neptune Family
Ryugu Kingdom</b>

96
00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:31.280
I hope that you can
answer an inquiry of mine.

97
00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:33.000
The princes are here!

98
00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.480
Ask me! Anything!

99
00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:35.800
They have princes?

100
00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.020
Sanji, no!

101
00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:40.450
U-Uh–

102
00:05:43.050 --> 00:05:44.840
Hide here and stay still!

103
00:05:45.930 --> 00:05:47.100
Hey, where...?

104
00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.320
I received a report that someone

105
00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:58.040
<b>Fukaboshi, First Son
(Shark Merman)</b>

106
00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:58.310
entered the city illegally.
Have they come by here, perhaps?

107
00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:00.720
If they have,
and you've seen them,

108
00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:03.750
<b>Ryuboshi, Second Son
(Oarfish Merman)</b>

109
00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:04.310
be sure to tell
♪ me-fa-so-la-ti-do! ♪

110
00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:06.900
♪ Mambo! Mambo!
Shakey, shakey moon fish! ♪

111
00:06:05.810 --> 00:06:09.820
<b>Manboshi, Third Son
(Opah Merman)</b>

112
00:06:06.900 --> 00:06:09.820
♪ Why we gotta do this?
Let's party with the ladies! ♪

113
00:06:09.820 --> 00:06:12.260
I'm sorry, but we haven't
seen anyone here.

114
00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:15.290
They sound like common thugs.
Are they really that important?

115
00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.420
Surely they don't
demand the attention

116
00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:18.780
of princes such as you!

117
00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:19.630
Perhaps.

118
00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:21.790
We have yet to ascertain
their identities,

119
00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:24.160
so it may be too early
to say just yet.

120
00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:26.500
♪ He doesn't know la-ti-do! ♪

121
00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:28.420
Who cares? Let's dance!

122
00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:29.170
Yay!

123
00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:32.380
♪ Ain't no party
like a mambo party! ♪

124
00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.320
What's all this commotion?

125
00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:40.260
Huh?

126
00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:43.950
Aw, man, it's the
princes from Neptune's army!

127
00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.320
What're they doing here?

128
00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.030
What a pain
in the ass. Now what?

129
00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:51.300
Let's see how it plays out.

130
00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:52.360
♪ Mambo, mambo, shake it! ♪

131
00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:55.930
Huh. I see. Well,
I thank you all.

132
00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:57.760
We shall search elsewhere.

133
00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.120
Forgive me for
interrupting your leisure.

134
00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.080
We'll dance again sometime!

135
00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:06.410
♪ And away we go-la-ti-do! ♪

136
00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:08.150
– Bye-bye!
– Bye-bye!

137
00:07:08.150 --> 00:07:10.910
Perhaps the border guards
were just seeing things.

138
00:07:10.910 --> 00:07:12.680
They're leaving.

139
00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:16.090
Soft– So soft–

140
00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:21.560
Big boobie! Big boobie!

141
00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:29.730
No! What did I do?

142
00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:32.500
That was too much blood!
He needs help, now!

143
00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:33.860
He's done for!

144
00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:36.410
All that pent-up lust
let loose in one shot!

145
00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:38.280
Sanji!

146
00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:42.210
Wait. No mistaking it.

147
00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:44.580
That's the pirate,
Straw Hat Luffy.

148
00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.650
<b>Ryugu Palace</b>

149
00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:48.740
Ammo Knights, go!

150
00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:49.320
– Yes, sir!
– Yes, sir!

151
00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:49.320
<b>Ryugu Palace</b>

152
00:08:03.930 --> 00:08:06.890
Well, look at than.
How convenient.

153
00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:09.340
I dunno. The guards
are gonna catch 'em first.

154
00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:11.350
Our orders are clear,
but we don't wanna

155
00:08:11.350 --> 00:08:13.710
start crap with
the Neptune Army.

156
00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:18.520
Wait, hold on a second... Please!

157
00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:19.820
We don't wanna fight!

158
00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:21.340
We can sort out
our crimes later,

159
00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:22.890
but right now,
there's an emergency!

160
00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:24.760
Our friend has lost
a lot of blood

161
00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:26.160
and we need a donor quick!

162
00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:28.770
If you leave him here,
or throw him in jail,

163
00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.630
he'll be dead within an hour.

164
00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:33.330
His blood type is S RH negative.

165
00:08:33.330 --> 00:08:35.900
I know it's rare, but does
someone here have it?

166
00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:38.240
Anyone? Fishmen
and humans do have

167
00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.250
the same kind of
blood, don't they?

168
00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:42.610
Chopper-chin.

169
00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:43.820
We don't have time!

170
00:08:43.820 --> 00:08:45.420
Guys, this is serious!

171
00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:48.110
Sanji! We are not
losing you over this!

172
00:08:48.850 --> 00:08:50.410
Please, I'm begging you!

173
00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:54.120
Whatever it takes!
I can't let my friend die!

174
00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:56.720
Chopper-chin. I'm sorry.

175
00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:59.170
Fishmen and humans do have
the same kind of blood,

176
00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:01.390
but the situation is complicated.

177
00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:02.330
The thing is—

178
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.330
Get a load of these humans!

179
00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:12.870
You really are
stupid, aren't ya?

180
00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:15.640
Weren't you a big enough
jerk the last time we met?

181
00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:18.910
His name is Hammond, sir.
He's from the Fishman District.

182
00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:20.140
Huh?

183
00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.540
You're not getting a damned drop

184
00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.500
from anybody on this island!

185
00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:26.800
Why would we share our blood

186
00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.420
with disgusting
creatures like you?

187
00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:30.610
Humans aren't worth
a thing down here.

188
00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:32.990
And even if someone
did help you,

189
00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:35.480
decent fishmen like us,
who hate humans,

190
00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:37.630
would make sure they
were punished for it.

191
00:09:37.630 --> 00:09:39.130
"Punished"?

192
00:09:39.130 --> 00:09:41.600
He can bleed out
right here, for all I care.

193
00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:44.330
Many fishmen would
happily watch him die!

194
00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:47.210
There's a law
for this, you know.

195
00:09:47.210 --> 00:09:49.210
One we've followed
for a long time.

196
00:09:49.210 --> 00:09:52.170
Fishmen are forbidden to
share blood with humans,

197
00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:53.310
no matter what.

198
00:09:53.970 --> 00:09:54.780
That law sucks!

199
00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:56.610
Don't blame me for it!

200
00:09:56.610 --> 00:10:00.350
After all, it was humans who set
the rule in the first place.

201
00:10:00.350 --> 00:10:02.140
Our blood may be the same,

202
00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:04.590
but for ages, you've
treated us like monsters,

203
00:10:04.590 --> 00:10:06.180
or worse, like animals.

204
00:10:06.180 --> 00:10:08.560
Your blood was too good for us!

205
00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:10.860
In fact, that's why
Fisher Tiger,

206
00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:13.330
the hero of this island, died.

207
00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:17.130
He said that name... once before.

208
00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:19.740
He fought to
free slaves of all races,

209
00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:22.230
and when that battle took
its toll on his body,

210
00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:24.000
when he lied bloody
and battered,

211
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:26.060
not a single human
would offer their blood

212
00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.940
to return his kindness.

213
00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:30.740
A transfusion
would've saved him,

214
00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:33.220
but 'cause of humans, he died!

215
00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:38.320
So right now, you
have but one choice.

216
00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:41.110
Well, it's not much
of a choice, really.

217
00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:43.310
Your friend is going to die,
and you're coming

218
00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:45.590
to the Fishman District with me!

219
00:10:45.590 --> 00:10:47.360
Hody Jones, the captain

220
00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:49.900
of the New Fishman Pirates,
is expecting you,

221
00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:52.470
and he doesn't like to wait!

222
00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:53.740
That's enough!

223
00:10:53.740 --> 00:10:56.970
Hey, who cares about some stupid
rule in the first place?

224
00:10:56.970 --> 00:10:58.550
You don't have to
listen to this thug!

225
00:10:58.550 --> 00:11:00.680
There's someone's life
on the line here!

226
00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:03.630
We'll do anything it
takes to repay you!

227
00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:05.950
Now is not the time
to get stuck on pride!

228
00:11:10.630 --> 00:11:11.120
Camie!

229
00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:12.860
Come along, Straw Hat!

230
00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:15.170
Now, Second Gear!

231
00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:19.760
I'll take you by
force if I have to!

232
00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:21.930
Trawl Net!

233
00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:25.070
I'm not joining
your stupid crew!

234
00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:27.500
I already told you, didn't I?

235
00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:29.010
Jet Pistol!

236
00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:31.510
Leave us alone!

237
00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:40.020
Get away!

238
00:11:40.020 --> 00:11:41.180
That thing is too big!

239
00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:52.800
My word, he made
quick work of them!

240
00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:54.190
It just gave up!

241
00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:57.170
I guess Luffy can tame
sea monsters now?

242
00:11:57.170 --> 00:11:58.400
Cool!

243
00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:00.740
What happened? That was crazy!

244
00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:03.370
Impressive.

245
00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:05.940
Luffy-chin! Up here!

246
00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:12.360
Bring Sanji-chin up here!

247
00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:13.690
We'll go back to town!

248
00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.320
There's lots of humans there,

249
00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:18.370
so might be able to
find a blood donor!

250
00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:19.060
Let's hurry!

251
00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:20.710
I'm coming!

252
00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:33.370
Cool! Ready to go!

253
00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:34.460
Thanks, Camie!

254
00:12:34.460 --> 00:12:37.170
Sure. We need
to head over to town.

255
00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:37.810
Is that okay?

256
00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:39.270
Mosu!

257
00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:42.460
Hey, you can't do that!
It belongs to the princes!

258
00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:43.710
I'm sorry, guys!

259
00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:46.550
We'll bring your ship back
as soon as we save Sanji-chin!

260
00:12:46.550 --> 00:12:48.650
And away they go!

261
00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:49.460
How are we supposed to

262
00:12:49.460 --> 00:12:51.960
get home now? So-la-ti-do!

263
00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:57.130
It's not fair.

264
00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.430
I'd do anything in the
world to save his life,

265
00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:00.830
but I don't have
the right blood type.

266
00:13:00.830 --> 00:13:03.420
No, it's nothing for
you to feel bad about.

267
00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:04.790
If he wasn't such a perv,

268
00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:06.800
this wouldn't have happened
in the first place.

269
00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:07.710
Look at him!

270
00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:10.300
He's dying and he's still
thinking about boobs.

271
00:13:10.300 --> 00:13:12.000
So bouncy.

272
00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.500
So soft and bouncy and...

273
00:13:14.500 --> 00:13:16.680
So soft and bouncy...
Stop! You're in
a delicate state!

274
00:13:16.680 --> 00:13:18.620
If you keep thinking
about dirty stuff,

275
00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:20.980
you're gonna lose what
little blood you have left!

276
00:13:22.840 --> 00:13:24.940
We may be friends,
but considering the way

277
00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:27.120
you and Hachi got
treated back on Sabaody,

278
00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:29.200
I should've guessed something
like this would happen.

279
00:13:29.200 --> 00:13:31.860
There's some deep-rooted
stuff going on here.

280
00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:35.020
Yeah. And to be honest,
I dunno how this'll go.

281
00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:37.590
There's no promise anyone'll
help us back in town.

282
00:13:37.590 --> 00:13:38.670
Huh?

283
00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:41.220
We're counting on
human donors for blood,

284
00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:43.720
but I haven't seen any
at all this past month.

285
00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:45.310
In fact, your ship
is the first one

286
00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:46.410
we've had in a long time.

287
00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:48.360
Why? I thought everyone

288
00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:49.520
had to come through here.

289
00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:51.810
Yeah, it wasn't
like this before.

290
00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:54.160
Nobody can say for
certain, but we think

291
00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:55.680
someone's attacking
the travelers,

292
00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:56.720
like what happened
with you guys.

293
00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:58.980
There's something going
on in this kingdom,

294
00:13:58.980 --> 00:14:01.820
and I have a sinking feeling
it's about to get ugly.

295
00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:07.930
Please, ladies,
you must be forthright.

296
00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:10.770
Why did you try to conceal
those pirates from us?

297
00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:14.840
We're sorry, Prince.
They aren't bad people.

298
00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:17.310
It sounds like what happened
wasn't their fault.

299
00:14:17.310 --> 00:14:19.330
They're Camie's friends,
and they got split up

300
00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:20.760
from their crew,
so we didn't want them

301
00:14:20.760 --> 00:14:22.750
to be thrown in jail
as soon as they got here.

302
00:14:22.780 --> 00:14:25.820
Don't be sad...
everybody!

303
00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:25.820
I hope they
find a donor for Sanji.

304
00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:27.980
Alas, you misunderstood us.

305
00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:30.320
Their method of entry
is no concern.

306
00:14:27.980 --> 00:14:27.980
Yeah, we have different
business with them

307
00:14:30.320 --> 00:14:31.580
They're quite famous.

308
00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:33.560
It would only be
a small formality.

309
00:14:33.560 --> 00:14:36.020
We don't consider them
enemies, after all.

310
00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.730
Yeah, we have different
business with them!

311
00:14:38.730 --> 00:14:41.530
♪ Re-mi-fa-so-la-ti ♪

312
00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:43.170
Then this is all our fault.

313
00:14:46.020 --> 00:14:48.510
We... had a message
to pass on to them.

314
00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:50.200
From Jinbe.

315
00:14:57.870 --> 00:14:59.930
Hey, that barrel over there
is the one that drifted

316
00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:01.640
in with all Camie's
friends, right?

317
00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:04.450
What's in it? Maybe treasure?

318
00:15:04.450 --> 00:15:06.090
Uh... I don't know.

319
00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:08.890
It's sealed pretty tightly,
so it's gotta be important.

320
00:15:09.300 --> 00:15:12.130
Yeah? I think we should open it.

321
00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:14.820
Me too. What if it
needs to go in the fridge?

322
00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:17.530
Good point!

323
00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:25.110
<b>"Coral Hill", Port Town
Ryugu Kingdom</b>

324
00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.820
Hey, Sanji! Are you awake?

325
00:15:30.820 --> 00:15:31.450
Talk to us.

326
00:15:33.720 --> 00:15:35.350
Where am I?

327
00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:38.350
You pulled through!

328
00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:40.480
We're safe in a town
right by the harbor.

329
00:15:40.480 --> 00:15:41.780
I was scared.

330
00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:44.060
You almost lost all
the blood in your body.

331
00:15:45.050 --> 00:15:46.200
I was starting to think

332
00:15:46.200 --> 00:15:50.080
we'd never find you a donor.
That was a real close call.

333
00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:51.770
That so? Wow.

334
00:15:54.560 --> 00:15:56.810
What in the hell happened to me?

335
00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:59.280
You shouldn't be
sitting up so quickly!

336
00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:00.610
You need to rest!

337
00:16:00.610 --> 00:16:02.160
I just don't get it.

338
00:16:02.160 --> 00:16:04.240
I mean, the fish
could've given blood.

339
00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:06.440
But no, instead we had
to run all over town

340
00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:09.420
looking for another human,
which took forever!

341
00:16:09.420 --> 00:16:10.510
I know. Right?

342
00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:11.960
I was starting
to lose hope there.

343
00:16:11.960 --> 00:16:13.260
I'm sorry.

344
00:16:13.260 --> 00:16:15.870
I appreciate what
you did, though.

345
00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:18.700
But I just don't remember much.

346
00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:19.940
Why'd this happen?

347
00:16:19.940 --> 00:16:22.020
Where was I, and
what was I doing?

348
00:16:22.020 --> 00:16:24.330
When I think about it,
it's all a big blur.

349
00:16:25.340 --> 00:16:25.710
No!

350
00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:27.250
– Let it go already!
– Let it go already!

351
00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:30.440
If you try to force the
memories, you could relapse!

352
00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:33.160
Oh, yeah! I almost
forgot, Sanji.

353
00:16:33.160 --> 00:16:34.800
You haven't met your donors.

354
00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.860
So, here. Say "hi."

355
00:16:38.480 --> 00:16:39.240
Wait.

356
00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:42.850
Could my savior have
been a dainty girl?

357
00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:46.140
Don't worry. We're only human.

358
00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:50.430
After all, if we don't look out
for each other, who will?

359
00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:53.180
Don't worry, babe.

360
00:16:53.740 --> 00:16:54.800
If you want...

361
00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:57.830
<b>Splash and Splatter
Pirate Twins</b>

362
00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:57.830
– ...we can give you more!
– ...we can give you more!

363
00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:07.510
Looks like he's
back to his old self!

364
00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:11.880
That's not exactly gratitude.

365
00:17:12.800 --> 00:17:13.850
Luffy...

366
00:17:13.860 --> 00:17:16.240
Can I see the cut on your
arm for a second, please?

367
00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:17.650
Uh?

368
00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:24.080
It's positive. Thought so.

369
00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:26.500
Luffy, that wound's poisonous!

370
00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:28.400
Oh, wow. Really?

371
00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:30.170
That musta been the
sting I felt earlier.

372
00:17:31.010 --> 00:17:32.570
One of the fishmen got me.

373
00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:35.220
You don't seem poisoned.

374
00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:36.660
You feeling okay?

375
00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:37.440
Yeah!

376
00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:39.110
Either way,
we should be careful.

377
00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:43.370
This stuff's probably deadly.
You sure you're all right?

378
00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:43.850
Yup.

379
00:17:43.850 --> 00:17:45.900
Wow. So weird.

380
00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:48.730
It sounds crazy, but you
must have somehow developed

381
00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:51.730
an antibody to fight against
this kind of stuff.

382
00:17:51.730 --> 00:17:52.530
Tell me.

383
00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:55.620
Have you ever experienced a
poisoning like this in the past?

384
00:17:55.620 --> 00:17:56.960
Let's see...

385
00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:03.030
Yeah, back when
I was at Impel Down,

386
00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:05.130
I almost got killed that way.

387
00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:10.940
That is... not funny... at all!

388
00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:12.600
Yeah! It is!

389
00:18:13.250 --> 00:18:15.660
I bet it was that
octopus swordsman.

390
00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:19.100
I mean, he blocked my punch.
So he's gotta be strong.

391
00:18:19.100 --> 00:18:21.720
No prob. Next time,
I'll be ready.

392
00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:29.600
Huh?

393
00:18:30.760 --> 00:18:32.930
They're so loud.

394
00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:36.540
I think that came
from by that cove.

395
00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:38.900
Don't care. I've got
bigger problems.

396
00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:42.100
These guys are
messed up real bad.

397
00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:46.850
And what's worse,
Straw Hat got poisoned too.

398
00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:48.460
<b>Hyozo, Assassin
New Fishman Pirates
(Blue-Ringed Octopus Merman)</b>

399
00:18:46.850 --> 00:18:48.960
I'm dead if he dies.

400
00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:52.780
I'm positive I heard their
screams come from here.

401
00:18:52.780 --> 00:18:54.430
Ishilly!

402
00:18:54.430 --> 00:18:55.810
– Where are you?
– Where are you?

403
00:18:56.790 --> 00:18:58.880
This is where I saw them last.

404
00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:00.840
But where in the world
could they have gone?

405
00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:02.560
Did anyone else
hear them say something

406
00:19:02.560 --> 00:19:04.230
about opening up a barrel?

407
00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:08.480
Hey, Luffy-chin,
Usopp-chin, come here.

408
00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:09.900
There's someone I'd
like you to meet.

409
00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:11.000
– Huh?
– Huh?

410
00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:15.320
She's the owner of this place.

411
00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:18.080
She okayed Sanji resting here.

412
00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:18.080
Look at this thing!

413
00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.800
The Madam Sharley.

414
00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:20.980
Cool, thanks and stuff.

415
00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:25.880
Has the blond
boy's condition improved at all?

416
00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:28.650
<b>Madame Sharley
Owner of the Mermaid Café</b>

417
00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:26.760
Yup!

418
00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:29.710
But it's best he doesn't meet
you because you're so beautiful.

419
00:19:29.710 --> 00:19:31.640
Right? That would be bad.

420
00:19:31.640 --> 00:19:33.400
Also, we probably
shouldn't tell him

421
00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:35.920
he's in the back
of the Mermaid Café.

422
00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:37.620
Not if we want him to get well.

423
00:19:37.620 --> 00:19:39.380
Why keep it a secret?

424
00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:40.730
'Cause doctor's orders!

425
00:19:40.730 --> 00:19:43.380
Chopper's pretty sure that
if Sanji-chin finds out,

426
00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:44.900
he's gonna have a bad relapse.

427
00:19:44.900 --> 00:19:47.440
What a strange prognosis.

428
00:19:48.340 --> 00:19:50.810
Hey, big lady!
Fish lady!

429
00:19:50.810 --> 00:19:53.480
Wow! That was rude. Come on!

430
00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:54.860
Tell me what this is!

431
00:19:54.860 --> 00:19:56.120
It's beautiful!

432
00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:58.230
It's also not
on the list of things

433
00:19:58.230 --> 00:19:59.370
you're allowed to touch.

434
00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:01.000
Oh, that?

435
00:20:01.000 --> 00:20:03.720
You're looking at Madam
Sharley's crystal ball.

436
00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:05.290
With it, she can see the future.

437
00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:08.000
Her precognitive visions
are why she's famous.

438
00:20:09.080 --> 00:20:12.190
Well, it used to be.
Not anymore.

439
00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:20.040
The future isn't ours
to know. Right?

440
00:20:21.210 --> 00:20:22.230
Sounds rough.

441
00:20:22.230 --> 00:20:25.110
Oh, by the way, how do
mermaids take a dump?

442
00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:27.540
We are not talking about
mermaid poop again!

443
00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:29.880
Don't you have any
CLAAAASS?!

444
00:20:29.880 --> 00:20:31.980
Guys, apologize! Quickly!

445
00:20:32.550 --> 00:20:33.460
– Sorry.
– Sorry.

446
00:20:34.180 --> 00:20:37.540
Why don't you take
the rest of the day off, Camie?

447
00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:40.720
I think your friends would
appreciate a tour of the island.

448
00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:42.570
Really? You sure?

449
00:20:42.570 --> 00:20:43.540
It's fine.

450
00:20:43.540 --> 00:20:46.390
You deserve it, seeing as
you're always working so hard.

451
00:20:47.140 --> 00:20:48.680
Besides, business has been slow

452
00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:50.980
with human guests so
uncommon these days.

453
00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:53.370
So we have to be
extra good hosts.

454
00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:55.500
The girls from the cove
should show up soon.

455
00:20:55.500 --> 00:20:58.040
Then we'll have more hands
around here than a starfish.

456
00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:01.780
"More than... starfish?"
Oh, that's right! Crap!

457
00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:04.850
I should have already delivered
Pappag's clams by now!

458
00:21:05.780 --> 00:21:07.850
Wow. I have no idea
what's going on.

459
00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:10.510
I bet he's getting mad
waiting for his food.

460
00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:13.010
Not quite. He's
enjoying the café.

461
00:21:13.010 --> 00:21:15.420
An old friend of his
suddenly came into town,

462
00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:17.560
and they've been living
it up since he arrived.

463
00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:19.020
Wait, he's here?

464
00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:21.290
– Well, that makes things easy.
– Well, that makes things easy.

465
00:21:26.940 --> 00:21:29.120
I didn't wanna bring
this up in front of her,

466
00:21:29.120 --> 00:21:30.780
but Madam told me
a lot of stories

467
00:21:30.780 --> 00:21:32.070
from when she was little.

468
00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.040
She said, in those days,

469
00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:36.110
human pirates came to
the island all the time.

470
00:21:36.680 --> 00:21:38.250
But that was quite a while ago.

471
00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:41.150
About a year before the
Great Pirate Era began.

472
00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:46.080
It's hard for her to
talk about things sometimes.

473
00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:48.160
Especially when she
foresees bad stuff,

474
00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:50.720
like the war at Marineford
and Whitebeard's death.

475
00:21:50.720 --> 00:21:51.970
– What?!
– What?!

476
00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:55.170
Can you imagine knowing
something horrible will happen

477
00:21:55.170 --> 00:21:56.160
that you can't stop?

478
00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:57.830
That must be terrifying!

479
00:21:57.830 --> 00:21:59.210
Hey, where's Chopper?

480
00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:01.250
Oh, he said he
was gonna hang out here

481
00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:02.270
and look after Sanji.

482
00:22:02.280 --> 00:22:03.960
C'mon, you two! Hurry up!

483
00:22:03.960 --> 00:22:04.660
– 'Kay!
– 'Kay!

484
00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:09.460
Right now, we're on
what's considered

485
00:22:09.460 --> 00:22:11.050
Coral Hill's main street.

486
00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:15.370
And that is the primary
entrance to the Mermaid Café.

487
00:22:17.920 --> 00:22:20.800
Man! Thought I was
gonna starve to death!

488
00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:22.330
They might only serve snacks.

489
00:22:22.570 --> 00:22:23.940
No. You're good.

490
00:22:23.940 --> 00:22:25.960
We've got cakes and
sea fruit too.

491
00:22:25.960 --> 00:22:26.890
And meat?

492
00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:28.220
Uh, no.

493
00:22:28.220 --> 00:22:31.260
We merfolk don't really
eat meat and fish.

494
00:22:31.260 --> 00:22:35.200
But we have wakame brûlée,
mozuku tarts, kelp soufflé...

495
00:22:35.510 --> 00:22:37.440
You call that food?

496
00:22:37.440 --> 00:22:39.800
Wait! We do have some meat!

497
00:22:40.490 --> 00:22:41.540
From shellfish!

498
00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:44.250
Scallop sandwiches,
clam pizza, and–

499
00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:45.850
Those give meat a bad name!

500
00:22:45.850 --> 00:22:47.150
Stop! Talking!

501
00:22:47.200 --> 00:22:49.460
Whoa. Okay. Be cool.

502
00:22:49.460 --> 00:22:50.550
Let's just go inside.

503
00:22:50.550 --> 00:22:52.890
Yeah. Let's all
go find Pappag.

504
00:22:52.890 --> 00:22:55.160
Shellfish! What the hell
kind of crap is that?

505
00:22:55.470 --> 00:22:57.060
– Thank you very much!
– Thank you very much!

506
00:22:57.060 --> 00:22:58.160
Yeah!

507
00:23:00.150 --> 00:23:02.420
Time to give the dogfish a bone!

508
00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:04.200
Gotta love the fans, huh?

509
00:23:04.200 --> 00:23:05.740
Oh, wow, it's Brook!

510
00:23:05.740 --> 00:23:06.840
Hooray!

511
00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:09.390
Huh? Luffy and Usopp!

512
00:23:09.390 --> 00:23:12.640
And Camie, you've become
such a lovely young lady!

513
00:23:12.980 --> 00:23:14.510
Hey, guys!

514
00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:16.780
You have no idea how
much I've missed you!

515
00:23:16.810 --> 00:23:18.110
Why didn't you
tell me you were coming?

516
00:23:18.380 --> 00:23:20.520
Hey, Pappag!
Sorry it's been so long!

517
00:23:20.520 --> 00:23:23.560
I guess that makes you Pappag's
old friend we heard about.

518
00:23:23.560 --> 00:23:25.460
Come see us again! 'Kay?

519
00:23:26.790 --> 00:23:28.960
I had a great time, Soul King!

520
00:23:31.130 --> 00:23:32.900
I'll be back,
lovely ladies!

521
00:23:32.900 --> 00:23:34.530
Lots of bones to go around!

522
00:23:34.530 --> 00:23:35.670
What?!

523
00:23:35.670 --> 00:23:37.030
I've gone limp!

524
00:23:39.330 --> 00:23:43.000
No, I haven't. Ha!
Skeletons are always rigid!

525
00:23:43.000 --> 00:23:45.500
Ah, good thing I'm already dead,

526
00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:48.140
or I would probably die
of embarrassment right now!

527
00:23:48.140 --> 00:23:49.580
– Oh, you!
– Oh, you!

528
00:23:49.580 --> 00:23:52.520
This café has really
put Brook in rare form.

529
00:23:52.520 --> 00:23:54.890
Yeah, whatever's goin' on
inside must be awesome!

530
00:23:54.890 --> 00:23:56.650
Hold up there, boss!

531
00:23:56.650 --> 00:23:57.750
– Huh?
– Huh?

532
00:23:57.750 --> 00:23:59.540
What're ya in such a hurry for?

533
00:23:59.540 --> 00:24:02.260
I know you're interested
in the café, and I get that,

534
00:24:02.260 --> 00:24:04.020
but it's not like
it's going anywhere.

535
00:24:04.020 --> 00:24:06.250
Let's come back when
you have your whole crew.

536
00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:09.140
Bone-Daddy and I were just
about to head back to my place.

537
00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:10.900
Why don't you guys come with us?

538
00:24:11.890 --> 00:24:15.280
If you do, you can eat all
the sea king meat you want!

539
00:24:15.280 --> 00:24:17.300
Did you say "meat"?

540
00:24:17.300 --> 00:24:21.040
Yeah, I did! I'm a wild
animal! Ya feel me?

541
00:24:21.040 --> 00:24:23.060
It's not like I eat
boring shellfish.

542
00:24:23.060 --> 00:24:25.200
I need food with
a little more bite.

543
00:24:25.200 --> 00:24:26.520
Sea monster exclusive diet!

544
00:24:26.980 --> 00:24:28.480
Oh! By the way,

545
00:24:28.980 --> 00:24:30.480
I brought your order of clams!

546
00:24:30.480 --> 00:24:33.370
Sweet! My favorite
treat is finally here!

547
00:24:33.370 --> 00:24:35.220
Ha! So much for your diet!

548
00:24:35.220 --> 00:24:36.690
Oh, man!

549
00:24:37.300 --> 00:24:39.710
Look, merfolk are the only
ones who don't eat meat.

550
00:24:39.710 --> 00:24:41.460
Fishmen eat the stuff
all the time!

551
00:24:41.460 --> 00:24:43.050
So it's not like you
can't get it here,

552
00:24:43.050 --> 00:24:44.660
it's just not as common.

553
00:24:44.660 --> 00:24:46.300
Yes! That's great!

554
00:24:46.300 --> 00:24:48.440
Man, it's about
time one of them showed up.

555
00:24:48.440 --> 00:24:49.600
Hey, taxi!

556
00:24:52.730 --> 00:24:54.580
Hey. Wait a minute!

557
00:24:57.210 --> 00:24:58.510
Vander Decken!
Thought so!

558
00:24:59.360 --> 00:25:01.880
But why is there a wanted
poster for a ghost?

559
00:25:01.880 --> 00:25:02.560
Yeah!

560
00:25:02.560 --> 00:25:04.950
Wasn't this guy on the
haunted ship we saw?

561
00:25:05.600 --> 00:25:07.400
You saw him? For real?

562
00:25:07.400 --> 00:25:08.120
Uh-huh.

563
00:25:08.120 --> 00:25:09.600
No way! Whoa!

564
00:25:09.600 --> 00:25:12.240
Our nation's been looking
for him for years now!

565
00:25:12.240 --> 00:25:15.270
The dude's a pirate and
a no-good undersea thief.

566
00:25:15.270 --> 00:25:17.080
I'll tell you all
about it on the trip.

567
00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:18.730
Let's load up and go!

568
00:25:23.610 --> 00:25:26.020
Story goes, Vander
Decken was hard up.

569
00:25:26.020 --> 00:25:27.660
The guy was totally
head-over-heels

570
00:25:27.660 --> 00:25:30.040
for the Mermaid Princess
of the Ryugu Kingdom.

571
00:25:30.040 --> 00:25:32.670
He was so desperate,
he sent love letters daily.

572
00:25:33.710 --> 00:25:35.760
Stalkery, y'know?

573
00:25:35.760 --> 00:25:39.120
Gave up letters. Started sending
gifts instead. Then threats.

574
00:25:39.120 --> 00:25:40.590
– So soft and fluffy!
– So soft and fluffy! Wanted to marry her.

575
00:25:40.590 --> 00:25:41.320
– Feels great!
– Feels great!

576
00:25:41.690 --> 00:25:44.180
And springy! Bouncy! Bouncy!

577
00:25:44.180 --> 00:25:46.400
Are you even listening to me?

578
00:25:46.400 --> 00:25:47.830
– Sure!
– Sure!

579
00:25:47.830 --> 00:25:48.900
Sorry about that.

580
00:25:48.900 --> 00:25:52.480
Ahem. Because his advances
started to become so violent,

581
00:25:52.480 --> 00:25:54.280
the Mermaid Princess got scared.

582
00:25:54.280 --> 00:25:57.960
And so of course, the stalker
became a national concern!

583
00:25:57.960 --> 00:26:00.490
Yeah! But that was
just the beginning!

584
00:26:00.490 --> 00:26:02.820
Her father,
King Neptune, got mad,

585
00:26:02.820 --> 00:26:05.500
which led to him sending the
three princes you saw earlier

586
00:26:05.500 --> 00:26:06.990
off to hunt Vander Decken.

587
00:26:06.990 --> 00:26:09.680
But even with the army,
they can't find him.

588
00:26:09.680 --> 00:26:13.520
Oh, c'mon, Camie.
You stole all my thunder.

589
00:26:13.520 --> 00:26:15.960
By the way! King Neptune's
the God of the Sea!

590
00:26:15.960 --> 00:26:17.960
Plus he's in control
of this country.

591
00:26:17.960 --> 00:26:19.880
If that's not enough
responsibility,

592
00:26:19.880 --> 00:26:22.060
he has four children
to take care of!

593
00:26:22.060 --> 00:26:24.340
The Mermaid Princess
is the youngest,

594
00:26:24.340 --> 00:26:26.780
so, obviously, the three
princes are the older kids

595
00:26:26.780 --> 00:26:27.900
in the royal family.

596
00:26:27.900 --> 00:26:30.070
Please. I got this.

597
00:26:30.070 --> 00:26:33.010
Great. But, something
still doesn't make sense.

598
00:26:33.010 --> 00:26:35.180
Vander Decken must be quite ancient

599
00:26:33.510 --> 00:26:35.180
What's goin' on down there?

600
00:26:35.180 --> 00:26:38.530
If he isn't a ghost, I imagine
he's a few hundred years old.

601
00:26:38.530 --> 00:26:39.750
At least!

602
00:26:39.750 --> 00:26:41.600
Huh. You're right,

603
00:26:41.600 --> 00:26:42.920
that doesn't make sense.

604
00:26:42.920 --> 00:26:45.590
That is, unless,
you ignore the rumors.

605
00:26:46.170 --> 00:26:48.220
Now there's no denying
that he existed.

606
00:26:48.220 --> 00:26:51.090
But the truth of the matter is
that the legendary sea captain

607
00:26:51.090 --> 00:26:53.940
Vander Decken died sometime
after he arrived here

608
00:26:53.940 --> 00:26:56.800
on Fishman Island and hasn't
been heard from since.

609
00:26:57.560 --> 00:26:59.720
That said, the ship
you say you saw

610
00:26:59.720 --> 00:27:02.220
probably was the
Flying Dutchman, but...

611
00:27:04.010 --> 00:27:06.210
It's his descendant
who's on board!

612
00:27:07.810 --> 00:27:08.360
He's–

613
00:27:08.360 --> 00:27:10.280
He's Vander Decken the Ninth!

614
00:27:12.650 --> 00:27:14.780
Wow! That's a lot!

615
00:27:14.210 --> 00:27:18.250
<b>Fish Taxi</b>

616
00:27:14.780 --> 00:27:15.820
Well, I have to say,

617
00:27:15.820 --> 00:27:18.600
it's a relief to find out
he's not a ghost after all.

618
00:27:18.600 --> 00:27:20.540
Believing we had come
into contact with someone

619
00:27:20.540 --> 00:27:23.660
from the afterlife was making me
contemplate my own mortality.

620
00:27:23.660 --> 00:27:26.870
And considering I'm a skeleton,
I don't have much of that left.

621
00:27:26.870 --> 00:27:29.680
I just wanted to tell
an exciting story.

622
00:27:29.680 --> 00:27:32.570
Man. I thought
merfolk and fishmen

623
00:27:32.570 --> 00:27:35.170
all looked the same, but the
more I see, the less they do.

624
00:27:35.170 --> 00:27:36.930
Check out those
old ones down there!

625
00:27:36.930 --> 00:27:39.370
Their fins are split
like Granny Kokoro!

626
00:27:39.370 --> 00:27:41.270
See those babies?
Right there.

627
00:27:42.620 --> 00:27:44.320
You'll notice
the father is a fishman,

628
00:27:44.320 --> 00:27:46.410
but the children are
a mix of both species.

629
00:27:46.840 --> 00:27:48.920
That's because when
a mermaid and a fishman

630
00:27:48.920 --> 00:27:51.580
love each other very much
and decide to get busy,

631
00:27:51.580 --> 00:27:53.680
their kids can come out
looking like either parent.

632
00:27:54.970 --> 00:27:57.500
Oh. That's why they
all look different.

633
00:27:57.500 --> 00:27:59.170
So cool!

634
00:27:59.170 --> 00:28:01.560
All right, we finally
made it to the highway!

635
00:28:05.210 --> 00:28:09.900
Whoa! This is fast!
What's up with that place?

636
00:28:09.900 --> 00:28:12.210
Oh. Nothing,
it's a candy factory.

637
00:28:12.210 --> 00:28:13.020
Really?

638
00:28:13.020 --> 00:28:15.080
Then why's there
a pirate flag on it?

639
00:28:15.080 --> 00:28:17.280
Oh, that? That flag's
everywhere here.

640
00:28:17.280 --> 00:28:20.170
By the entrance and the
harbor. It's a big deal!

641
00:28:20.170 --> 00:28:21.630
And for good reason at that.

642
00:28:21.630 --> 00:28:24.230
It symbolizes that
we're protected.

643
00:28:24.230 --> 00:28:26.950
Y'see, the flag belongs
to a famous pirate

644
00:28:26.950 --> 00:28:29.060
named Charlotte Linlin
of the New World.

645
00:28:29.270 --> 00:28:32.760
But she's better known as Big
Mom, one of the Four Emperors!

646
00:28:32.760 --> 00:28:34.700
Whoa. That's no joke.

647
00:28:34.700 --> 00:28:37.340
Ah. Back before
the war in Marineford,

648
00:28:37.340 --> 00:28:39.100
Whitebeard was this
island's guardian,

649
00:28:39.100 --> 00:28:41.890
but now that he's dead, someone
else had to take his place.

650
00:28:41.890 --> 00:28:44.480
And that someone
happened to be her.

651
00:28:44.480 --> 00:28:46.100
Okay.

652
00:28:46.100 --> 00:28:48.970
The thing is, she
demands a whole ton of candy

653
00:28:48.970 --> 00:28:50.900
in exchange for her services.

654
00:28:50.900 --> 00:28:52.960
Hence the factory
that you just saw.

655
00:28:52.960 --> 00:28:54.150
That's weird.

656
00:28:54.150 --> 00:28:56.330
This country wouldn't
be able to survive

657
00:28:56.330 --> 00:28:58.690
without the protection of
powerful people like her.

658
00:28:58.690 --> 00:29:01.590
After all, this is a dangerous
place where pirates come and go,

659
00:29:01.590 --> 00:29:04.090
and more often than not,
they aren't very friendly.

660
00:29:04.090 --> 00:29:05.260
Yeah, I guess.

661
00:29:05.260 --> 00:29:07.700
Plus, she's filling in
where Whitebeard left off,

662
00:29:07.700 --> 00:29:09.630
so that's gotta mean she's
a good person, doesn't it?

663
00:29:10.220 --> 00:29:11.810
Depends on how you look at it.

664
00:29:11.810 --> 00:29:13.340
Whitebeard never
asked for anything

665
00:29:13.340 --> 00:29:14.910
in return for his protection.

666
00:29:14.910 --> 00:29:16.120
Big Mom, on the other hand,

667
00:29:16.120 --> 00:29:18.360
treats it like a business
rather than a charity.

668
00:29:18.360 --> 00:29:20.040
Still. That's cool.

669
00:29:20.040 --> 00:29:23.070
An Emperor. Like Shanks! Crazy!

670
00:29:23.070 --> 00:29:24.280
Hope I get to meet her.

671
00:29:24.790 --> 00:29:26.360
Eyes forward!

672
00:29:26.360 --> 00:29:28.730
This is where all the
celebrity types live:

673
00:29:28.730 --> 00:29:30.220
Fishverly Hills!

674
00:29:31.620 --> 00:29:34.170
That tall building right
in front is Pappag's house,

675
00:29:34.170 --> 00:29:35.660
where we're going!

676
00:29:35.660 --> 00:29:38.630
– All that for one starfish?
– All that for one starfish?

677
00:29:40.980 --> 00:29:42.630
<b>Coral Hill</b>

678
00:29:44.870 --> 00:29:46.560
We have to do something!

679
00:29:46.560 --> 00:29:48.400
We can't let this happen!

680
00:29:48.400 --> 00:29:51.460
That's Madam Sharley
from the café.

681
00:29:51.460 --> 00:29:53.900
What's the matter?
Please. Please tell us.

682
00:29:53.900 --> 00:29:55.810
What's wrong? Why are you upset?

683
00:29:55.810 --> 00:29:59.080
Something must be done.
Now, before it's too late!

684
00:29:59.080 --> 00:30:01.480
Uh. Sure. What do we do?

685
00:30:03.910 --> 00:30:07.180
Find him!
The pirate boy in a straw hat!

686
00:30:07.180 --> 00:30:08.940
It's an emergency!

687
00:30:10.400 --> 00:30:12.020
He must leave the country!

688
00:30:12.020 --> 00:30:13.730
Now! There's no time!

689
00:30:13.860 --> 00:30:15.930
Wait. You're having
a premonition?

690
00:30:15.930 --> 00:30:18.200
I swore I wouldn't
use this power.

691
00:30:18.200 --> 00:30:20.810
But something about
that boy felt off to me.

692
00:30:20.810 --> 00:30:25.070
I... I had no choice
but to look into the future!

693
00:30:26.170 --> 00:30:29.360
What's going to happen?!
Tell us! What did you see?!

694
00:30:29.360 --> 00:30:30.910
We have to know!

695
00:30:31.310 --> 00:30:33.080
Sharley! Tell us!

696
00:30:33.430 --> 00:30:34.400
Madam!

697
00:30:34.400 --> 00:30:35.280
Please!

698
00:30:36.380 --> 00:30:39.720
I hope I'm wrong,
and that it won't happen!

699
00:30:46.430 --> 00:30:49.880
I saw him clearly,
surrounded by flames.

700
00:30:51.130 --> 00:30:53.840
Because of Straw Hat Luffy,

701
00:30:53.840 --> 00:30:57.070
Fishman Island,
our country will be...

702
00:30:59.930 --> 00:31:01.710
destroyed!
